{"audit_run_id":"audit:60c88de2e1d3434d92e1413032b03337","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":97,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"One row is one randomised patient: an adult with chronic insomnia disorder enrolled in the sleep"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"clinic trial, with the support they were randomised to and their week-eight outcome values. There"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"are 70 rows, one per patient, 35 in each group. Every patient has a value for every outcome; there"},{"end_column":47,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"are no missing cells and no repeated patients."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"The four sleep-diary outcomes are each the patient's average over a two-week diary kept at week"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"eight. The insomnia severity index score is taken from one questionnaire completed at week eight."},{"end_column":60,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"The file has a header row and seven columns, in this order."},{"end_column":32,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"| Column | Type | Description |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":150,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| `patient_id` | text | Patient identifier: the prefix `P` plus a zero-padded two-digit serial number, `P01` through `P70`. Unique within the file. |"},{"end_column":253,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| `group` | text | Which support the patient was randomised to. Exactly two distinct values: `booklet` (sleep-hygiene information booklet, no guidance) and `digital_cbti` (six-week guided digital cognitive behavioural therapy programme for insomnia). |"},{"end_column":157,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| `sleep_onset_latency_min` | integer | Declared outcome 1. Sleep onset latency: minutes from lights out to falling asleep, rounded to the nearest minute. |"},{"end_column":185,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `wake_after_sleep_onset_min` | integer | Declared outcome 2. Wake after sleep onset: minutes spent awake between falling asleep and the final waking, rounded to the nearest minute. |"},{"end_column":129,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `total_sleep_time_min` | integer | Declared outcome 3. Total sleep time per night in minutes, rounded to the nearest minute. |"},{"end_column":144,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `sleep_efficiency_pct` | number, one decimal place | Declared outcome 4. Sleep efficiency: total sleep time as a percentage of time in bed. |"},{"end_column":169,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `insomnia_severity_index_score` | integer | Declared outcome 5. Insomnia severity index total score on the 0 to 28 scale, where a higher score means worse insomnia. |"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"Columns 3 through 7 are the five outcome variables of the declared outcome family, listed here in"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"the order the protocol declared them."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"These are whole-file ranges across all 70 patients, given so a reader can see the scale of each"},{"end_column":8,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"column."},{"end_column":31,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"| Column | Minimum | Maximum |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":40,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| `sleep_onset_latency_min` | 12 | 86 |"},{"end_column":44,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"| `wake_after_sleep_onset_min` | 12 | 136 |"},{"end_column":39,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"| `total_sleep_time_min` | 249 | 493 |"},{"end_column":41,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"| `sleep_efficiency_pct` | 56.0 | 94.9 |"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"| `insomnia_severity_index_score` | 3 | 28 |"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"- The values are fixed and committed in the CSV. Nothing in the analysis is generated at run time."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"- The diary quantities for a patient are internally consistent: sleep efficiency is total sleep time"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":47,"start_column":3,"start_line":47,"text":"as a share of that patient's time in bed, and time in bed also covers the sleep onset latency, the"},{"end_column":71,"end_line":48,"start_column":3,"start_line":48,"text":"wake after sleep onset, and any time awake in bed before getting up."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:2bdafa93038460b8c68a","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:af6257c0692908df0aed6c61980e33afa498f250810df8739a7eeb0312508489","end_line":48,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-48","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:60c88de2e1d3434d92e1413032b03337","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":93,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `group` column of `sleep_study_data.csv`."},{"end_column":186,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: sleep_onset_latency_min, wake_after_sleep_onset_min, total_sleep_time_min, sleep_efficiency_pct, insomnia_severity_index_score."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:d5f5df21d9b013d744c8","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:1c740d439eea2f53e8c0553941554a684ec0367f601d364cc0828fa6114f3c4c","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
