{"audit_run_id":"audit:60c88de2e1d3434d92e1413032b03337","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":93,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Adults with chronic insomnia disorder attending a sleep clinic were randomised to one of two"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"supports, and the study asks which of the two leaves patients sleeping better at week eight. The"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"two supports are the only comparison in the study:"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"- **Booklet.** A sleep-hygiene information booklet, given with no guidance."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":10,"start_column":1,"start_line":10,"text":"- **Digital CBT-I.** A six-week guided digital cognitive behavioural therapy programme for"},{"end_column":12,"end_line":11,"start_column":3,"start_line":11,"text":"insomnia."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"Seventy patients were randomised, thirty-five to each support. Outcomes were taken at week eight"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"from a two-week sleep diary and one questionnaire."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"The data file is `sleep_study_data.csv`. **One row is one randomised patient**, holding the support"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"that patient was randomised to and that patient's week-eight outcome values. There are 70 rows, 35"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"per group, with no missing cells and no repeated patients. The four sleep-diary outcomes are each"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"the patient's average over the two-week diary; the insomnia severity index score comes from the"},{"end_column":33,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"single week-eight questionnaire."},{"end_column":28,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"The file has seven columns:"},{"end_column":25,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| Column | Description |"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| --- | --- |"},{"end_column":60,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `patient_id` | Patient identifier, `P01` through `P70`. |"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"| `group` | The support the patient was randomised to: `booklet` or `digital_cbti`. |"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"| `sleep_onset_latency_min` | Declared outcome 1. Minutes from lights out to falling asleep. |"},{"end_column":114,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"| `wake_after_sleep_onset_min` | Declared outcome 2. Minutes awake between falling asleep and the final waking. |"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"| `total_sleep_time_min` | Declared outcome 3. Minutes of sleep per night. |"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"| `sleep_efficiency_pct` | Declared outcome 4. Total sleep time as a percentage of time in bed. |"},{"end_column":115,"end_line":34,"start_column":1,"start_line":34,"text":"| `insomnia_severity_index_score` | Declared outcome 5. Insomnia severity index total, 0 to 28, higher is worse. |"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"Columns 3 through 7 are the five outcome variables of the declared outcome family, in the order the"},{"end_column":24,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"protocol declared them."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two supports with an independent two-sample t-test, run on the"},{"end_column":37,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"five outcomes in the declared order."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"Five outcomes were declared as **one outcome family** in the protocol, fixed before randomisation."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"Testing five outcomes at the conventional 0.05 level would inflate the family-wise error rate, so"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"the conventional family-wise level of 0.05 is divided across the five outcomes: 0.05 / 5 = 0.01."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"That is the Bonferroni-corrected per-outcome level. This **0.01 threshold was fixed in the protocol"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"in advance**, before any patient was recruited, and every one of the five outcomes is judged against"},{"end_column":54,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"it. No other threshold is used anywhere in the study."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"The analysis script `analysis.py` uses that 0.01 threshold as the protocol gives it; the arithmetic"},{"end_column":82,"end_line":52,"start_column":1,"start_line":52,"text":"that produced it is stated here in the report rather than recomputed in the code."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"Group means are arithmetic means over the 35 patients in each group. P-values are from the"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":57,"start_column":1,"start_line":57,"text":"independent two-sample t-test, and each verdict is against the protocol threshold of 0.01."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"Booklet mean 44.97, digital CBT-I mean 28.49, a difference of 16.49 minutes shorter on the"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"programme. p = 0.0000076. **Significant** at 0.01."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"Booklet mean 62.63, digital CBT-I mean 45.31, a difference of 17.31 minutes less time awake on the"},{"end_column":48,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"programme. p = 0.0030. **Significant** at 0.01."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":71,"start_column":1,"start_line":71,"text":"Booklet mean 372.86, digital CBT-I mean 394.29, a difference of 21.43 minutes more sleep on the"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"programme. p = 0.065. **Not significant** at 0.01."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":76,"start_column":1,"start_line":76,"text":"Booklet mean 75.74, digital CBT-I mean 83.13, a difference of 7.39 percentage points higher on the"},{"end_column":49,"end_line":77,"start_column":1,"start_line":77,"text":"programme. p = 0.00011. **Significant** at 0.01."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":81,"start_column":1,"start_line":81,"text":"Booklet mean 17.03, digital CBT-I mean 11.40, a difference of 5.63 points lower, meaning less severe"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":82,"start_column":1,"start_line":82,"text":"insomnia, on the programme. p = 0.000000058. **Significant** at 0.01."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":86,"start_column":1,"start_line":86,"text":"Against the pre-specified 0.01 threshold, the guided digital CBT-I programme beats the unguided"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":87,"start_column":1,"start_line":87,"text":"booklet on four of the five declared outcomes. Patients on the programme fall asleep sooner, spend"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":88,"start_column":1,"start_line":88,"text":"less time awake during the night, use a higher share of their time in bed asleep, and report less"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":89,"start_column":1,"start_line":89,"text":"severe insomnia. Total sleep time was the one outcome that did not clear the threshold: the"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":90,"start_column":1,"start_line":90,"text":"programme group slept about 21 minutes more per night on average, but that difference was not"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":91,"start_column":1,"start_line":91,"text":"significant at 0.01. The pattern is what a sleep-restriction and stimulus-control programme would be"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":92,"start_column":1,"start_line":92,"text":"expected to produce, with the gains showing up in the quality and continuity of sleep rather than in"},{"end_column":18,"end_line":93,"start_column":1,"start_line":93,"text":"its total length."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:4a58e46e26ec22d0a7d3","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:66711ee5dcab714e341f237d12f81dbe9c81ce37887f89c035f29b8e189139a5","end_line":93,"locator":"report.md:1-93","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
